#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:17
msgid ""
"It is required to run the tests from a phpBB clone of the git repository, "
"because the test framework is not included in the download packages."
msgstr ""
"Det er påkrævet at køre testene fra en phpBB-klon af git-repositoryet, fordi"
" testframeworket ikke er inkluderet i download-pakkerne."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:21
msgid "Unit Tests"
msgstr "Unit tests"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:23
msgid ""
"Since unit tests are explained in more detail in the "
":doc:`../testing/unit_testing` section of the general testing documentation "
"and require no changes for extensions, we only add a quick example here."
msgstr ""
"Da unit tests forklares mere detaljeret i afsnittet "
":doc:`../testing/unit_testing` i den generelle testdokumentation og ikke "
"kræver ændringer for udvidelser, tilføjer vi kun et hurtigt eksempel her."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:29
msgid ""
"If you have not yet run the tests of phpBB, it is recommended to make a "
"break here and try to run them first. This helps to make sure, you have set "
"up everything correctly, before writing the tests for the extension."
msgstr ""
"Hvis du endnu ikke har kørt phpBB's tests, anbefales det at holde en pause "
"her og prøve at køre dem først. Dette hjælper med at sikre, at du har sat "
"alt korrekt op, før du skriver testene til udvidelsen."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:33
msgid ""
"More details are explained in the :doc:`../testing/unit_testing` section."
msgstr "Flere detaljer forklares i afsnittet :doc:`../testing/unit_testing`."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:146
msgid "Using mocks"
msgstr "Brug af mocks"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:148
msgid ""
"In the ``setUp()`` method we create our controller object. However, we do "
"not use the actual phpBB classes which are used by the controller when "
"opening the page. Instead `phpunit mocks "
"<https://phpunit.readthedocs.io/en/7.5/test-doubles.html>`_ are injected."
msgstr ""
"I metoden ``setUp()`` opretter vi vores controller-objekt. Vi bruger dog "
"ikke de egentlige phpBB-klasser, som bruges af controlleren, når siden "
"åbnes. I stedet injiceres `phpunit mocks "
"<https://phpunit.readthedocs.io/en/7.5/test-doubles.html>`_."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:154
msgid ""
"These mocks allow us to check how often a method is called, what the "
"arguments are and let us specify the return value. This helps us to verify "
"that **our** controller code behaves as expected. These mocks also help "
"prevent getting false errors in cases where using the actual phpBB classes "
"may behave unexpectedly."
msgstr ""
"Disse mocks giver os mulighed for at kontrollere, hvor ofte en metode "
"kaldes, hvad argumenterne er, og lader os angive returværdien. Dette hjælper"
" os med at verificere, at **vores** controller-kode opfører sig som "
"forventet. Disse mocks hjælper også med at forhindre falske fejl i tilfælde,"
" hvor brug af de egentlige phpBB-klasser kan opføre sig uventet."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:161
msgid "Testing a method"
msgstr "Test af en metode"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:163
msgid ""
"In our controller we added special handling when the provided name is "
"``bertie``. So our first test is whether the "
"``phpbb\\controller\\helper::message()`` method is called **once** with the "
"``NO_AUTH_SPEAKING`` error message. We also want to make sure that the "
"``phpbb\\controller\\helper::render()`` method is not called in this case."
msgstr ""
"I vores controller tilføjede vi speciel håndtering, når det angivne navn er "
"``bertie``. Så vores første test er, om metoden "
"``phpbb\\controller\\helper::message()`` kaldes **én gang** med "
"fejlmeddelelsen ``NO_AUTH_SPEAKING``. Vi vil også sikre os, at metoden "
"``phpbb\\controller\\helper::render()`` ikke kaldes i dette tilfælde."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:169
msgid ""
"Then we call the controller's ``handle()`` method. If the methods are "
"invoked correctly the test will pass."
msgstr ""
"Derefter kalder vi controllerens metode ``handle()``. Hvis metoderne kaldes "
"korrekt, vil testen bestå."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:190
msgid ""
"Make sure that the name of your testing method starts with ``test``. "
"Otherwise the test will not be executed by phpunit."
msgstr ""
"Sørg for, at navnet på din testmetode starter med ``test``. Ellers vil "
"testen ikke blive eksekveret af phpunit."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:194
msgid "Data providers"
msgstr "Data providers"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:196
msgid ""
"In most cases we will want to provide some test data to our unit test "
"methods. A data provider is a method that returns an array of arrays "
"containing input variables and expected output variables. The inner array "
"contains the arguments for the ``test`` method."
msgstr ""
"I de fleste tilfælde vil vi gerne levere nogle testdata til vores unit test-"
"metoder. En data provider er en metode, der returnerer et array af arrays, "
"der indeholder inputvariabler og forventede outputvariabler. Det indre array"
" indeholder argumenterne til ``test``-metoden."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:211
msgid ""
"This data provider contains two arrays of test data, so our test will be "
"called twice, once with the arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Denne data provider indeholder to arrays af testdata, så vores test kaldes "
"to gange, én gang med argumenterne:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:214
msgid "'foo'"
msgstr "'foo'"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:215
msgid "true"
msgstr "true"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:216
msgid "'DEMO_GOODBYE'"
msgstr "'DEMO_GOODBYE'"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:218
msgid "and a second time with:"
msgstr "og en anden gang med:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:220
msgid "'bar'"
msgstr "'bar'"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:221
msgid "false"
msgstr "false"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:222
msgid "'DEMO_HELLO'"
msgstr "'DEMO_HELLO'"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:224
msgid ""
"In the test we then tell the ``phpbb\\config\\config`` mock to expect to be "
"called only once, and to return the specified value (which is passed in as "
"an argument) for the ``acme_demo_goodbye`` config variable."
msgstr ""
"I testen fortæller vi derefter mock'en ``phpbb\\config\\config``, at den kun"
" skal forvente at blive kaldt én gang, og at den skal returnere den angivne "
"værdi (som sendes ind som et argument) for config-variablen "
"``acme_demo_goodbye``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:242
msgid ""
"If we have a short look at our controller again, we see that the value of "
"the config influences the ``\\phpbb\\language\\language::lang()`` call:"
msgstr ""
"Hvis vi kigger kort på vores controller igen, kan vi se, at config-værdien "
"påvirker kaldet til ``\\phpbb\\language\\language::lang()``:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:250
msgid ""
"This is what we check with the third argument ``$expected_language`` of our "
"test method:"
msgstr ""
"Dette er det, vi kontrollerer med det tredje argument ``$expected_language``"
" i vores testmetode:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:260
msgid ""
"For more information about Mocks and phpunit, please have a look at the "
"`phpunit Documentation <https://phpunit.readthedocs.io/en/7.5/test-"
"doubles.html>`_."
msgstr ""
"For flere oplysninger om mocks og phpunit, se venligst `phpunit-"
"dokumentationen <https://phpunit.readthedocs.io/en/7.5/test-doubles.html>`_."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:264
msgid "phpunit configuration file"
msgstr "phpunit-konfigurationsfil"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:266
msgid ""
"Before we can run the tests we need to create the configuration file for "
"phpunit. Don't be scared if you do not understand it, you should not need to"
" edit anything in that file. The file should be stored as "
"``ext/acme/demo/phpunit.xml.dist``:"
msgstr ""
"Før vi kan køre testene, skal vi oprette konfigurationsfilen til phpunit. "
"Bliv ikke forskrækket, hvis du ikke forstår den, du bør ikke behøve at ændre"
" noget i den fil. Filen bør gemmes som ``ext/acme/demo/phpunit.xml.dist``:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:308
msgid ""
"Now we can finally run the test suite by executing the following command:"
msgstr "Nu kan vi endelig køre testsuiten ved at eksekvere følgende kommando:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:314
#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:335
msgid "Results:"
msgstr "Resultater:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:329
msgid ""
"To run only the tests from one file just append the relative path to the "
"call:"
msgstr ""
"For kun at køre testene fra én fil skal du blot tilføje den relative sti til"
" kaldet:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:352
msgid "Unit tests with database interaction"
msgstr "Unit tests med databaseinteraktion"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:354
msgid ""
"When testing your own tables and columns, you can not use the normal "
"database that phpBB's unit tests set up by default."
msgstr ""
"Når du tester dine egne tabeller og kolonner, kan du ikke bruge den normale "
"database, som phpBB's unit tests opsætter som standard."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:358
msgid "Migration with database changes"
msgstr "Migrering med databaseændringer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:360
msgid ""
"Our extension has a migration file "
"``ext/acme/demo/migrations/add_database_changes.php``, which contains some "
"database changes, so we can test them:"
msgstr ""
"Vores udvidelse har en migreringsfil "
"``ext/acme/demo/migrations/add_database_changes.php``, som indeholder nogle "
"databaseændringer, så vi kan teste dem:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:432
msgid "Testing database changes"
msgstr "Test af databaseændringer"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:434
msgid ""
"If we add a new test that checks for the existence of the table, we will see"
" that the test fails:"
msgstr ""
"Hvis vi tilføjer en ny test, der kontrollerer, om tabellen findes, vil vi "
"se, at testen fejler:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:490
msgid ""
"Before we can run the database test, we need to create the fixture file we "
"specified in the ``getDataSet()`` method. This file can be used to create "
"database entries before each test run is executed. We will make use of this "
"later. For now we just want to check if our tables have been created, so we "
"specify an empty config table "
"``ext/acme/demo/tests/migrations/database/fixtures/add_database_changes.xml``:"
msgstr ""
"Før vi kan køre databasetesten, skal vi oprette fixture-filen, vi angav i "
"metoden ``getDataSet()``. Denne fil kan bruges til at oprette "
"databaseposter, før hver testkørsel udføres. Vi vil gøre brug af dette "
"senere. For nu vil vi blot kontrollere, om vores tabeller er blevet "
"oprettet, så vi angiver en tom config-tabel "
"``ext/acme/demo/tests/migrations/database/fixtures/add_database_changes.xml``:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:509
msgid "Execution"
msgstr "Eksekvering"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:511
msgid "When we now execute the tests again they will fail:"
msgstr "Når vi nu eksekverer testene igen, vil de fejle:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:542
msgid ""
"In order to get our database changes executed in unit tests, we need to tell"
" phpBB that this test needs the extension to be set up. We can do this by "
"overwriting the ``\\phpbb_database_test_case::setup_extensions()`` method of"
" the test and returning an array with the extension name:"
msgstr ""
"For at få vores databaseændringer eksekveret i unit tests skal vi fortælle "
"phpBB, at denne test kræver, at udvidelsen er sat op. Vi kan gøre dette ved "
"at overskrive testens metode "
"``\\phpbb_database_test_case::setup_extensions()`` og returnere et array med"
" udvidelsens navn:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:558
msgid "and now the test passes successfully:"
msgstr "og nu består testen korrekt:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:576
msgid ""
"As you can see, the time for the test execution went up from a few hundred "
"milliseconds to a few seconds. This is because database tests set up the "
"database and populate it, which just takes time."
msgstr ""
"Som du kan se, steg tiden for testeksekveringen fra nogle hundrede "
"millisekunder til nogle få sekunder. Dette skyldes, at databasetests "
"opsætter databasen og fylder den med data, hvilket simpelthen tager tid."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:580
msgid ""
"Therefore it is recommended to only use database tests when you really need "
"the database. It is better to split your test file into a database-test and "
"a non-database one, to keep the run time short."
msgstr ""
"Det anbefales derfor kun at bruge databasetests, når du virkelig har brug "
"for databasen. Det er bedre at opdele din testfil i en databasetest og en "
"ikke-databasetest for at holde kørselstiden kort."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:585
msgid "Using fixtures"
msgstr "Brug af fixtures"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:587
msgid ""
"Now let's make use of the fixture file to populate the database for our "
"test. Therefore we replace the content of the "
"``ext/acme/demo/tests/migrations/database/fixtures/add_database_changes.xml``"
" file with the following content:"
msgstr ""
"Lad os nu gøre brug af fixture-filen til at fylde databasen med data til "
"vores test. Vi erstatter derfor indholdet af filen "
"``ext/acme/demo/tests/migrations/database/fixtures/add_database_changes.xml``"
" med følgende indhold:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:612
msgid ""
"You can leave out columns from the tables, if you do not want to specify "
"values for them."
msgstr ""
"Du kan udelade kolonner fra tabellerne, hvis du ikke ønsker at angive "
"værdier for dem."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:617
msgid ""
"Database columns that are specified as ``TEXT_UNI`` columns need to be "
"specified, otherwise your test will fail on some databases."
msgstr ""
"Databasekolonner, der er angivet som ``TEXT_UNI``-kolonner, skal angives, "
"ellers vil din test fejle på nogle databaser."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:620
msgid ""
"After we added the content to the database we add a new test at the end of "
"the file, that queries our table to the "
"``ext/acme/demo/tests/migrations/database/add_database_changes.php`` and "
"tests whether the values are really in the database:"
msgstr ""
"Efter vi har tilføjet indholdet til databasen, tilføjer vi en ny test i "
"slutningen af filen, der forespørger vores tabel til "
"``ext/acme/demo/tests/migrations/database/add_database_changes.php`` og "
"tester, om værdierne virkelig findes i databasen:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:660
msgid "Functional testing"
msgstr "Funktionel testning"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:662
msgid ""
"Functional tests simulate calling a URL and allow you to filter the output "
"then and check whether certain elements have a specific content."
msgstr ""
"Funktionelle tests simulerer at kalde en URL og giver dig mulighed for "
"derefter at filtrere outputtet og kontrollere, om bestemte elementer har et "
"specifikt indhold."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:667
msgid ""
"Again it is recommended to run the functional tests of phpBB first, before "
"writing the tests for the extension."
msgstr ""
"Igen anbefales det at køre phpBB's funktionelle tests først, før du skriver "
"testene til udvidelsen."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:670
msgid ""
"More details are explained in the :doc:`../testing/functional_testing` "
"section."
msgstr ""
"Flere detaljer forklares i afsnittet :doc:`../testing/functional_testing`."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:673
msgid ""
"Again like with the database changes we need to tell phpBB that the test "
"depends on the extension, then phpBB will take care of enabling the "
"extension before the test execution. Our little test opens the route we "
"added and then checks for the right message, like the unit test we wrote in "
"`unit tests`_ at the beginning:"
msgstr ""
"Igen, ligesom med databaseændringerne, skal vi fortælle phpBB, at testen "
"afhænger af udvidelsen, hvorefter phpBB tager sig af at aktivere udvidelsen "
"før testeksekveringen. Vores lille test åbner den route, vi tilføjede, og "
"kontrollerer derefter den rigtige besked, ligesom den unit test, vi skrev i "
"`unit tests`_ i begyndelsen:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:722
msgid "Running this test, however, will fail:"
msgstr "At køre denne test vil dog fejle:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:750
msgid ""
"The reason is that the test suite compares the response for the correct "
"format (valid HTML, without debug errors) and a successful status code "
"``200``."
msgstr ""
"Grunden er, at testsuiten sammenligner svaret for det korrekte format "
"(gyldig HTML, uden fejlfindingsfejl) og en vellykket statuskode ``200``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:753
msgid ""
"Therefore we need to adjust the bertie test, because we return a ``403`` "
"status in the controller, if someone tries to talk to bertie:"
msgstr ""
"Vi skal derfor justere bertie-testen, fordi vi returnerer en ``403``-status "
"i controlleren, hvis nogen forsøger at tale med bertie:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:767
msgid "Now the tests will pass correctly:"
msgstr "Nu vil testene bestå korrekt:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:785
msgid ""
"Functional tests are **slow**. Depending on your server, it might take up to"
" 2 seconds per page view. phpBB is installed via page views as well, which "
"takes another 20 to 100 seconds, depending on various configurations, for "
"the first functional tests. Subsequent functional tests **do not reinstall**"
" the board, so they do not have the long setup time."
msgstr ""
"Funktionelle tests er **langsomme**. Afhængigt af din server kan det tage op"
" til 2 sekunder pr. sidevisning. phpBB installeres også via sidevisninger, "
"hvilket tager yderligere 20 til 100 sekunder, afhængigt af forskellige "
"konfigurationer, for de første funktionelle tests. Efterfølgende "
"funktionelle tests **geninstallerer ikke** forummet, så de har ikke den "
"lange opsætningstid."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:792
msgid "Continuous integration with Github Actions"
msgstr "Continuous integration med GitHub Actions"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:794
msgid ""
"As a final step in this tutorial, we want to explain how to set up automated"
" testing of your extension using Github Actions. In order to do that, your "
"extension must first be set up as a project repository on `GitHub "
"<https://github.com>`_ (free of charge for public open source repositories)."
msgstr ""
"Som et sidste trin i denne tutorial vil vi forklare, hvordan man opsætter "
"automatiseret testning af din udvidelse ved hjælp af GitHub Actions. For at "
"gøre dette skal din udvidelse først opsættes som et projekt-repository på "
"`GitHub <https://github.com>`_ (gratis for offentlige open source-"
"repositories)."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:799
msgid ""
"If you need help setting up git and creating your GitHub project, please "
"have a look at the `Help section <https://help.github.com/>`_ on Github, "
"particularly the following two help topics:"
msgstr ""
"Hvis du har brug for hjælp til at opsætte git og oprette dit GitHub-projekt,"
" se venligst `hjælpesektionen <https://help.github.com/>`_ på GitHub, især "
"de følgende to hjælpeemner:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:803
msgid "`Set Up Git <https://help.github.com/articles/set-up-git>`_"
msgstr "`Set Up Git <https://help.github.com/articles/set-up-git>`_"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:804
msgid "`Create A Repo <https://help.github.com/articles/create-a-repo>`_"
msgstr "`Create A Repo <https://help.github.com/articles/create-a-repo>`_"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:808
msgid ""
"It is recommended to use the root of the extension (``ext/acme/demo``) as "
"the root for the Git repository. Otherwise the scripts that phpBB provides "
"for easy test execution on Travis CI will not work correctly."
msgstr ""
"Det anbefales at bruge udvidelsens rod (``ext/acme/demo``) som roden for "
"Git-repositoryet. Ellers vil de scripts, som phpBB leverer til nem "
"testeksekvering på Travis CI, ikke fungere korrekt."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:812
msgid ""
"View one of phpBB's official extension repositories as an example: `Board "
"Rules <https://github.com/phpbb-extensions/boardrules>`_."
msgstr ""
"Se et af phpBB's officielle udvidelses-repositories som eksempel: `Board "
"Rules <https://github.com/phpbb-extensions/boardrules>`_."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:816
msgid "Create your Github Action Workflow file"
msgstr "Opret din GitHub Action-workflow-fil"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:818
msgid ""
"From your repository on GitHub.com, click **Add File** and select **Create "
"new file** and name the file ``.github/workflows/tests.yml``."
msgstr ""
"Fra dit repository på GitHub.com skal du klikke på **Add File**, vælge "
"**Create new file** og navngive filen ``.github/workflows/tests.yml``."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:821
msgid "Copy the following into the ``tests.yml`` file:"
msgstr "Kopiér følgende ind i filen ``tests.yml``:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:849
msgid ""
"You must change the ``EXTNAME`` variable to your extension's name (as you "
"defined it in your composer.json file) in the ``with`` section at the bottom"
" of this file."
msgstr ""
"Du skal ændre variablen ``EXTNAME`` til navnet på din udvidelse (som du "
"definerede det i din composer.json-fil) i ``with``-sektionen nederst i denne"
" fil."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/tutorial_testing.rst:852
msgid ""
"To save and run your workflow, scroll to the bottom of the page and select "
"**Create a new branch for this commit and start a pull request**. Then, to "
"create a pull request, click **Propose new file**. After you merge this pull"
" request, all future commits and pull requests on your master branch will "
"trigger this CI workflow and your unit, database and functional tests will "
"be executed."
msgstr ""
"For at gemme og køre din workflow skal du rulle til bunden af siden og vælge"
" **Create a new branch for this commit and start a pull request**. For at "
"oprette en pull request skal du derefter klikke på **Propose new file**. Når"
" du har merget denne pull request, vil alle fremtidige commits og pull "
"requests på din master-branch udløse denne CI-workflow, og dine unit-, "
"database- og funktionelle tests vil blive eksekveret."

